        "original_id": "18976567-38f1-5474-a2cf-bd49ee65a9ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Birds of Steel\n- Companies: Gaijin Entertainment, Konami\n- Places: Pearl Harbor, Wake Island\n- Events: attack on Pearl Harbor, World War II\n- Topics: combat flight simulator video games\n\nFacts:\n- On December 7, 1941, the Empire of Japan attacked Pearl Harbor, and that attack was the immediate cause of the United States entering World War II.\n- Birds of Steel is a combat flight simulator video game created by Gaijin Entertainment and published by Konami.\n- Birds of Steel was released on March 13, 2012, for PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360.\n- Birds of Steel includes more than 100 non-fictional planes, 20 historical missions, and hundreds of procedural missions across 16 locations, including Pearl Harbor and Wake Island.",
